cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the note below."
title: "The Mirror Clause of the Geometric Selection Conjecture Is Empty: note, source and check"
abstract: >-
  The note proves that the fixed-point clause of the Geometric Selection
  Conjecture is never satisfied: a heterotic vacuum fixed by the mirror
  involution has a threefold isomorphic to its mirror, hence equal Hodge
  numbers, vanishing Euler number and a bundle with c_3 = 0 on its component,
  so it has no net families and fails the three-family condition. The
  conjecture is therefore equivalent to the existence of one viable vacuum on
  a component of the landscape carrying no standard embedding, with no
  condition involving mirror symmetry. The repository holds the note, its
  LaTeX source and the check of the lemma on Hodge data.
